diff --git a/features/clear-completed.feature b/features/clear-completed.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ec78672
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/clear-completed.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+Feature: Clear completed button
+  As a user
+  I want to remove all completed todos at once
+  So that I can clean up the list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy milk     |
+      | Walk the dog |
+      | Read book    |
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when nothing is completed
+    Then the clear completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button appears when something is completed
+    Given the user marks "Buy milk" as complete
+    Then the clear completed button is visible
+
+  Scenario: Clicking clear completed removes only the completed todos
+    Given the user marks "Buy milk" as complete
+    And the user marks "Read book" as complete
+    When the user clicks the clear completed button
+    Then "Buy milk" does not appear in the list
+    And "Read book" does not appear in the list
+    And "Walk the dog" still appears in the list
+    And the clear completed button is hidden
+    And the mark-all checkbox is unchecked
diff --git a/features/counter.feature b/features/counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7676130
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+Feature: Active todo counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many todos are still active
+  So that I know how much work remains
+
+  Scenario Outline: Counter pluralizes the count
+    Given the app is loaded with <count> todos titled "Task"
+    Then the active counter shows "<text>"
+
+    Examples:
+      | count | text          |
+      | 0     | 0 items left  |
+      | 1     | 1 item left   |
+      | 3     | 3 items left  |
+
+  Scenario: The count number is wrapped in a strong tag
+    Given the app is loaded with 1 todo titled "Buy milk"
+    Then the active counter wraps the number 1 in a strong tag
diff --git a/features/empty-state.feature b/features/empty-state.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1b7db34
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/empty-state.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Feature: Empty state
+  As a user
+  I want the app to start with a clean empty view
+  So that nothing distracts me before I add my first todo
+
+  Scenario: New app hides the main section and the footer
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Adding the first todo reveals the main section and the footer
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "Buy milk" into the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
+    And the todo list contains "Buy milk"
diff --git a/features/item.feature b/features/item.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8f7b41c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/item.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+Feature: Item interactions
+  As a user
+  I want to toggle, edit, and remove individual todos
+  So that I can manage my list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy milk     |
+      | Walk the dog |
+
+  Scenario: Clicking an item checkbox marks the todo complete
+    When the user marks "Buy milk" as complete
+    Then "Buy milk" has the completed state
+    And "Walk the dog" does not have the completed state
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label activates editing
+    When the user double-clicks the label of "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit updates the todo title
+    Given "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user changes the title to "Buy organic milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy organic milk"
+    And "Buy milk" does not appear in the list
+    And "Buy milk" is no longer in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Saving an empty edit destroys the todo
+    Given "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then "Buy milk" does not appear in the list
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Escape during editing discards the change
+    Given "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user changes the title to "Buy organic milk" and presses Escape
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And "Buy organic milk" does not appear in the list
+    And "Buy milk" is no longer in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the destroy button removes the todo
+    When the user clicks the destroy button on "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" does not appear in the list
+    And "Walk the dog" still appears in the list
diff --git a/features/mark-all.feature b/features/mark-all.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0db4aaf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/mark-all.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+Feature: Mark all as complete
+  As a user
+  I want a single checkbox to toggle every todo
+  So that I can update many items at once
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy milk     |
+      | Walk the dog |
+      | Read book    |
+
+  Scenario: Toggling the mark-all checkbox completes every todo
+    When the user clicks the mark-all checkbox
+    Then every todo in the list has the completed state
+
+  Scenario: Toggling the mark-all checkbox when all complete unmarks every todo
+    Given every todo in the list has the completed state
+    When the user clicks the mark-all checkbox
+    Then no todo in the list has the completed state
+
+  Scenario: The mark-all checkbox reflects the all-complete state
+    Given every todo in the list has the completed state
+    Then the mark-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: The mark-all checkbox is unchecked when any todo is incomplete
+    Given one todo in the list has the completed state and the others do not
+    Then the mark-all checkbox is unchecked
diff --git a/features/new-todo.feature b/features/new-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..15fb852
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/new-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+Feature: New todo
+  As a user
+  I want to add new todos by typing into the top input
+  So that I can capture what I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+
+  Scenario: Entering text and pressing Enter creates the todo
+    When the user enters "Walk the dog" into the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+    And the new todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario Outline: Empty or whitespace-only input does not create a todo
+    When the user enters <input> into the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+    Examples:
+      | input |
+      | ""    |
+      | "   " |
+
+  Scenario: Multiple todos appear in the order they were entered
+    When the user enters "First" into the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user enters "Second" into the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user enters "Third" into the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows "First", "Second", and "Third" in that order
+
+  Scenario: The new todo input receives focus on load
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the new todo input has focus
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3608556
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive a page reload
+  So that I do not lose work between sessions
+
+  Scenario: Todos are saved to localStorage under the framework key
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "Buy milk" into the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then localStorage has a key named "todos-vanilla"
+
+  Scenario: Each stored todo carries id, title, and completed fields
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "Buy milk" into the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the stored entry at "todos-vanilla" exposes id, title, and completed fields
+    And the stored entry at "todos-vanilla" has title "Buy milk" and completed false
+
+  Scenario: Reloading restores the todos
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy milk     |
+      | Walk the dog |
+    When the page reloads
+    Then the todo list shows "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted across reload
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos:
+      | title    |
+      | Buy milk |
+    And "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the page reloads
+    Then "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2284691
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Feature: Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the list by status using the URL
+  So that I can focus on what matters now
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy milk     |
+      | Walk the dog |
+      | Read book    |
+    And the user marks "Walk the dog" as complete
+
+  Scenario: The default route shows every todo
+    Given the user is on the default route
+    Then the todo list shows "Buy milk", "Walk the dog", and "Read book"
+
+  Scenario: The active route shows only active todos
+    When the user navigates to the active route
+    Then the todo list shows "Buy milk" and "Read book"
+    And "Walk the dog" does not appear in the list
+
+  Scenario: The completed route shows only completed todos
+    When the user navigates to the completed route
+    Then the todo list shows "Walk the dog"
+    And "Buy milk" does not appear in the list
+    And "Read book" does not appear in the list
+
+  Scenario: An item updated while filtered is hidden when it no longer matches the filter
+    Given the user is on the active route
+    When the user marks "Buy milk" as complete
+    Then "Buy milk" does not appear in the list
+
+  Scenario: The active filter link carries the selected class
+    When the user navigates to the completed route
+    Then the completed filter link has the selected class
+    And the all filter link does not have the selected class
+    And the active filter link does not have the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is persisted across reload
+    Given the user is on the active route
+    When the page reloads
+    Then the todo list shows "Buy milk" and "Read book"
+    And the active filter link has the selected class
